<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Shared Apple Info.plist additions. Tauri auto-discovers this file next to
  tauri.conf.json and MERGES it into the generated bundle Info.plist — for the
  macOS desktop bundle AND (alongside Info.ios.plist) the iOS build.

  These two TCC usage strings are the macOS counterpart to the entitlements in
  Entitlements.plist: under Hardened Runtime, mic/camera need BOTH the
  entitlement and a usage string or the OS silently denies the request on a
  signed build. iOS already declares identical strings in
  gen/apple/corvux_iOS/Info.plist, so the wording here is kept byte-identical —
  the shared-file merge is a no-op on iOS and adds the strings on macOS.

  (ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption — the held iOS export-compliance key — also
  belongs in this file once legal decides; it is harmless on the macOS
  Developer-ID build. See docs/ios-todo.md P0.)
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Corvux uses the camera only when you tap "Scan QR code" to pair a device for sync. It reads the pairing code shown on your other device — nothing is recorded or saved.</string>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Corvux uses your microphone only when you tap the voice-memo button. The recording is saved as an attachment in your vault. No background or always-on listening.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
